{#- Home: the front door, not a CV. It answers one question -- who is he, and what question animates his
    work -- on the wireframe of the site's external review (astra) as the controller took it under the
    owner's delegation (owner ruling 18 and controller decision C1, 2026-09-25/26; record kept privately):
    the masthead with the mark above the name; a short personal About; the featured paper, drawn from the
    first research card so that nothing is written twice; one dated Now line; the three latest news items
    with the rest behind an expander; and two invitations, to Teaching and to the Commonplace. The Research
    hand-off row that used to stand under "Elsewhere on this site" is the featured block now, and the heading
    is gone. Every word still comes from site.yaml; this file holds markup only. -#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}

{% block identity %}
    <div class="masthead">
{# alt="" on purpose: the portrait stands beside the name, and a description would make a screen reader say
   "Itamar Avitan" twice (deep review 2026-09-25, PA-05). The accessibility statement says so; change both. #}
      <picture><source srcset="{{ site.portrait.webp|local(base) }}" type="image/webp"><img src="{{ site.portrait.jpg|local(base) }}" width="120" height="120" alt=""></picture>
{# The mark above the name (owner: yes, Q-L masthead question, 2026-09-25; the WP-S14 spec, built here): the
   same row of three shapes the favicon and the colophon are made from, small, on the name's own column, so
   the front door opens and closes on the site's signature. aria-hidden: the colophon's copy carries the
   caption that says what it is, and the name is the next word. #}
      <div class="masthead__name"><svg class="mark mark--mast" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 42 10" width="50" height="12"><circle cx="5" cy="5" r="5"/><circle cx="21" cy="5" r="5"/><rect x="32" width="10" height="10"/></svg><h1>{{ site.name }}</h1></div>
      {{ m.role_line()|trim }}
{# The identity line (owner ruling 17, 2026-09-25): one string in site.yaml, so the meta description, the og
   text and the JSON-LD carry it whole. Here its first sentence is the lede and the second, the question,
   stands under it one step smaller: split at the first sentence end, and printed whole when there is none. #}
{% set said = site.identity_line.partition(". ") %}
      <p class="lede">{{ said[0] }}{{ said[1]|trim }}{% if said[2] %} <span class="lede__more">{{ said[2] }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
{# The address, and beside it the two profiles a recruiter and a peer open first. The full row of six stands
   in the colophon of every page, this one included: see the note over `contact` in macros.html.j2. The two
   labels are the exact ones in site.yaml's `links`; a label that is not there is silently not drawn. #}
      {{ m.contact("Contact", reach=true, profiles=false, pick=["GitHub", "Google Scholar"])|trim }}
    </div>
{% endblock %}

{# The margin rule on the front door starts at Now, not at About (controller decision C5 item 17 under owner
   ruling 18, 2026-09-25: the rule is kept where the content is dated and dropped where it is not; external
   review 2 §7 asked for About to read as prose and the featured paper as a visual explanation). main opens
   on plain paper, and each ruled section draws its own stretch of the rule -- Now, News and the invitations,
   down to the colophon's "Last updated" -- which is what a phone already does, one log at a time. About and
   the featured paper stand without the rule and without its section tick. #}
{% block main_class %} class="opens-plain"{% endblock %}
{% block main %}

    <section id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
      <h2 id="about-h" class="inset">About</h2>
      <div class="prose inset">
{% for paragraph in site.about %}
        <p>{{ m.nb(paragraph) }}</p>
{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>

{# The featured paper: the first research card's own badge, short title, four sentences (`feature` in
   site.yaml: question, test, result with its chance baseline, scope), the four marks of its diagram with
   one-word captions, and its Paper, Code and video buttons -- every piece read off the card, so the front
   door cannot drift from the research page. The title leads to the card on that page; the last link to the
   page itself. A card without `feature` draws no block; one without badges or buttons draws no badge or no
   links (build renders with StrictUndefined, so every key is tested first). The venue badge is the first
   badge without " · ", the card's own condition, so a presentation badge never takes the box here.
   What a screen reader hears: the title link names its page in a hidden span, as the invitations do; the
   Paper, Code and Video links carry the card's own `context` the same way (deep review 2026-09-25, PA-05). #}
{% if research and research[0].get("feature") %}
{% set card = research[0] %}
{% set feature = card.feature %}
{% set venue = namespace(badge=none) %}
{% for badge in card.get("badges") or [] %}{% if venue.badge is none and " · " not in badge %}{% set venue.badge = badge %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    <section id="research" aria-labelledby="research-h">
      <h2 id="research-h" class="inset">Research</h2>
      <div class="feature">
{% if venue.badge %}
        <p class="feature__venue"><span class="tag tag--venue">{{ venue.badge }}</span></p>
{% endif %}
        <div class="feature__body">
          <h3><a href="{{ 'research/#papers'|local(base) }}">{{ m.nb(card.title.split(": ", 1)[-1]) }}<span class="vh"> (Research page)</span></a></h3>
          <p class="feature__text">{{ m.nb(feature.question) }} {{ m.nb(feature.test) }} {{ m.nb(feature.result) }} {{ m.nb(feature.scope) }}</p>
{% if feature.get("stages") %}
          <ol class="recovery-diagram recovery-diagram--small" role="list" aria-label="The model-recovery test in four stages">
{% for stage in feature.stages %}
            <li>{{ m.recovery_mark(loop.index) }}<p>{{ m.nb(stage) }}</p></li>
{% endfor %}
          </ol>
{% endif %}
{# A list, not a line of prose with typed dots: the separator is drawn by the stylesheet in each item's left
   padding and clipped where an item opens a line, so no line ever ends or opens on a bare "·" -- the role
   line's mechanism (review of WP-S17, 2026-09-26: at 320-410px the row broke after "Video ·", and at 200%
   text the dot stood alone on a line of its own). role="list" as on the role line: Safari drops the list
   semantics of a list without markers, and a screen reader then hears the links without their count. #}
          <ul class="feature__links" role="list">
{% for label, shown in [("Paper", "Paper"), ("Code", "Code"), ("NeurIPS 2025 video", "Video")] %}
{% for button in card.get("buttons") or [] if button.label == label %}
            <li><a href="{{ button.url }}">{{ shown }}{% if button.get("context") %}<span class="vh"> {{ button.context }}</span>{% endif %}</a></li>
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
            <li><a href="{{ 'research/'|local(base) }}">More on the research page</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
{% endif %}

{# What he is doing at the moment, dated, so it is read as a snapshot and not as a standing claim. The date
   takes the gutter and its tick like every other date on the site. One line is a paragraph in the text
   column; two or more are one dotted list there, because none of them is an event with a date of its own. #}
    <section id="now" class="ruled" aria-labelledby="now-h">
      <h2 id="now-h" class="inset">Now</h2>
      <ul class="log" role="list">
        <li class="row">
          {{ m.dates(site.now_as_of, "when") }}
{% if site.now|length == 1 %}
          <p class="what">{{ m.nb(site.now[0]) }}</p>
{% else %}
          <ul class="what now" role="list">
{% for line in site.now %}
            <li>{{ m.nb(line) }}</li>
{% endfor %}
          </ul>
{% endif %}
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="news" class="ruled" aria-labelledby="news-h">
      <h2 id="news-h" class="inset">News</h2>
      <ul class="log log--tight" role="list">
        {{ m.news_rows(news_shown)|trim }}
      </ul>
{% if news_older %}
      <details class="older">
        <summary><span>Older news ({{ news_older|length }})</span></summary>
        <ul class="log log--tight" role="list">
          {{ m.news_rows(news_older)|trim }}
        </ul>
      </details>
{% endif %}
    </section>

{# The two invitations, to the pages that are about the person rather than the work: two rows on the grid,
   the page's name in the gutter as a tag rather than a date, a real thing from the page as the link and one
   clause on what else is there -- see the note over `elsewhere` in site.yaml for why the rows take no tick
   and no heading. aria-label, because the section has no heading of its own to be labelled by. #}
{% if site.get("elsewhere") %}
    <section id="elsewhere" class="invitations ruled" aria-label="Elsewhere on this site">
      <ul class="log log--tight log--go" role="list">
        {{ m.elsewhere_rows(site.elsewhere)|trim }}
      </ul>
    </section>
{% endif %}

{% endblock %}
